hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27913","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Mansur informed us, from Ata, from Habibah bint Maysarah, from Umm Kurz al-Kabiyyah al-Khuzaiyyah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning the aqiqah, and he said: For the boy, two equivalent sheep, and for the girl, one sheep."
"27915","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Ata narrated to me, from Habibah bint Maysarah, from Umm Bani Kurz al-Kabiyyah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: For the boy, two sheep, and for the girl, one sheep."
"27916","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata informed me, from Habibah bint Maysarah ibn Abi Khuthaym, from Umm Bani Kurz al-Kabiyyah, that she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the aqiqah, and he said: For the boy, two equivalent sheep, and for the girl, one sheep. I said to Ata: What are the two equivalent. He said: The two alike. Hajjaj said in his hadith: And sheep are dearer to me than goats, and he mentioned that she is dearer to me than its females. He said: And we like that he make its blackness thereof."
"27917","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid informed me, from Siba ibn Thabit, that Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Siba informed him that Umm Kurz informed him that she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the aqiqah, and he said: Two sheep are slaughtered for the boy, and one for the female, and it does not harm you whether they are males or females."
"27918","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid informed me that Siba ibn Thabit ibn Amr, from Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Siba, informed him that Umm Kurz informed him that she asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the aqiqah, and then he mentioned it."
